# Bazel's package traversal does not consult .gitignore, so `bazel build
# //...` recurses into anything on disk. Claude Code keeps git worktrees
# under .claude/worktrees/ — each one a full checkout carrying BUILD.bazel
# files and its own bazel-* convenience symlinks — and loading those as
# packages of THIS workspace breaks //... outright (measured: rules_shell's
# external test tree, reached through a worktree's bazel-* symlink, fails
# loading in seconds). .bazelignore is the only fence Bazel offers here.
.claude
